# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Kaligiran {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantum-HPC integration challenge {#the-quantum-hpc-integration-challenge}"
msgstr "Ang hamon sa integrasyon ng quantum-HPC {#the-quantum-hpc-integration-challenge}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "High-performance computing (HPC) workflows often require seamless coordination between classical compute clusters and quantum processing units (QPUs). Different quantum hardware backends and services expose distinct authentication mechanisms, wire formats, and job lifecycle APIs. Integrating IBM Quantum systems into HPC workload managers (such as Slurm) requires a clean, standard interface for resource acquisition, job execution, and session management.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga high-performance computing (HPC) workflow ay kadalasang nangangailangan ng maayos na koordinasyon sa pagitan ng mga classical compute cluster at quantum processing unit (QPU). Ang iba't ibang quantum hardware backend at serbisyo ay may kanya-kanyang authentication mechanism, wire format, at job lifecycle API. Ang pag-integrate ng mga IBM Quantum system sa mga HPC workload manager (tulad ng Slurm) ay nangangailangan ng malinis at standard na interface para sa resource acquisition, job execution, at session management.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What QRMI is {#what-qrmi-is}"
msgstr "Ano ang QRMI {#what-qrmi-is}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)** is a middleware library written in Rust that standardizes access to quantum hardware from HPC schedulers and classical applications. It exposes a single unified lifecycle API:\n"
msgstr "Ang **Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)** ay isang middleware library na isinulat sa Rust na nagpapa-standardize ng access sa quantum hardware mula sa mga HPC scheduler at classical application. Naglalantad ito ng iisang unified lifecycle API:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "QRMI is published as an open-source project at [github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi) and is described in the overview paper [arXiv:2506.10052](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10052).\n"
msgstr "Ang QRMI ay pinapublish bilang isang open-source project sa [github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi) at inilalarawan sa overview paper na [arXiv:2506.10052](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10052).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key design choices {#key-design-choices}"
msgstr "Mga pangunahing desisyon sa disenyo {#key-design-choices}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Resource lifecycle, not circuit compilation.** QRMI handles the acquire/submit/poll/release lifecycle and nothing else. Circuit compilation, optimization, and transpilation remain in the application layer (for example, Qiskit). This keeps the interface minimal and composable.\n"
msgstr "**Resource lifecycle, hindi circuit compilation.** Ang QRMI ay humahawak lamang ng acquire/submit/poll/release lifecycle at wala nang iba pa. Ang Circuit compilation, optimization, at transpilation ay nananatili sa application layer (halimbawa, Qiskit). Pinapanatili nito ang interface na minimal at composable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Vendor portability model.** While QRMI provides common job-management calls (`acquire`, `task_start`, `task_status`, `task_result`, `release`) across supported hardware backends, changing vendors also requires different compilation passes, vendor-specific payload construction, and result decoding in the application layer.\n"
msgstr "**Vendor portability model.** Bagama't ang QRMI ay nagbibigay ng karaniwang job-management call (`acquire`, `task_start`, `task_status`, `task_result`, `release`) sa lahat ng suportadong hardware backend, ang pagpalit ng vendor ay nangangailangan din ng ibang compilation pass, vendor-specific payload construction, at result decoding sa application layer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Native IBM payload format.** For IBM Quantum backends, QRMI uses OpenQASM 3 JSON payloads (`QiskitPrimitive`) conforming to the Qiskit Runtime schema.\n"
msgstr "**Native na IBM payload format.** Para sa mga IBM Quantum backend, gumagamit ang QRMI ng OpenQASM 3 JSON payload (`QiskitPrimitive`) na sumusunod sa Qiskit Runtime schema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Configuration through environment variables.** Credentials and endpoint URLs are read from environment variables at runtime. In an HPC cluster, the Slurm QRMI SPANK plugin sets these automatically when a job is dispatched. In a notebook or interactive session, you load them from a `.env` file. Application code never contains hardcoded credentials or endpoint URLs.\n"
msgstr "**Configuration sa pamamagitan ng environment variable.** Ang mga credential at endpoint URL ay binabasa mula sa environment variable sa runtime. Sa isang HPC cluster, awtomatikong itinatakda ito ng Slurm QRMI SPANK plugin kapag na-dispatch ang isang job. Sa isang notebook o interactive session, ilo-load mo ang mga ito mula sa isang `.env` file. Ang application code ay hindi kailanman naglalaman ng hardcoded na credential o endpoint URL.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**HPC scheduler integration through GRES.** When a Slurm job requests quantum resources using the QRMI SPANK plugin interface (`#SBATCH --gres=qpu:1` and `#SBATCH --qpu=ibm_kingston`), the plugin injects `QRMI_JOB_QPU_RESOURCES` and `QRMI_JOB_QPU_TYPES` into the job environment. Applications call `get_job_qpu_resources_and_types()` to discover which resources were allocated &mdash; no hardcoded backend names required. `QRMIService` wraps this pattern for Qiskit users.\n"
msgstr "**Integrasyon ng HPC scheduler sa pamamagitan ng GRES.** Kapag humiling ang isang Slurm job ng quantum resource gamit ang QRMI SPANK plugin interface (`#SBATCH --gres=qpu:1` at `#SBATCH --qpu=ibm_kingston`), ini-inject ng plugin ang `QRMI_JOB_QPU_RESOURCES` at `QRMI_JOB_QPU_TYPES` sa job environment. Tinatawag ng mga application ang `get_job_qpu_resources_and_types()` upang malaman kung aling mga resource ang na-allocate &mdash; walang kinakailangang hardcoded na pangalan ng backend. Ang `QRMIService` ay bumabalot sa pattern na ito para sa mga user ng Qiskit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The core API calls {#the-core-api-calls}"
msgstr "Ang mga pangunahing API call {#the-core-api-calls}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Call | Purpose |\n"
"|------|---------|\n"
"| `qrmi.acquire()` | Acquire access to the resource (for example, opens a dedicated session); returns a lock token |\n"
"| `qrmi.target()` | Retrieve backend capabilities (qubits, gates, coupling map) as JSON |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_start(payload)` | Submit a quantum job; returns a job ID |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_status(job_id)` | Poll job status (`Queued`, `Running`, `Completed`, `Failed`) |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_result(job_id)` | Retrieve completed job results as a raw JSON string |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_stop(job_id)` | Cancel or clean up a job |\n"
"| `qrmi.release(lock)` | Release the resource lock (for example, closes the session) |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Tawag | Layunin |\n"
"|------|---------|\n"
"| `qrmi.acquire()` | Kumuha ng access sa resource (halimbawa, nagbubukas ng dedicated session); nagbabalik ng lock token |\n"
"| `qrmi.target()` | Kumuha ng mga kakayahan ng backend (qubits, gates, coupling map) bilang JSON |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_start(payload)` | Magsumite ng quantum job; nagbabalik ng job ID |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_status(job_id)` | I-poll ang status ng job (`Queued`, `Running`, `Completed`, `Failed`) |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_result(job_id)` | Kumuha ng nakumpletong resulta ng job bilang raw JSON string |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_stop(job_id)` | Kanselahin o linisin ang isang job |\n"
"| `qrmi.release(lock)` | I-release ang resource lock (halimbawa, isinasara ang session) |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
