#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale examples {#small-scale-examples}"
msgstr "Mga maliliit na halimbawa {#small-scale-examples}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1–3 introduce the QRMI API by using simple circuits. Each step maps to a core phase of the QRMI lifecycle against IBM Quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "Ipinakikilala ng Hakbang 1–3 ang QRMI API gamit ang mga simpleng circuit. Bawat hakbang ay tumutugma sa isang pangunahing yugto ng QRMI lifecycle laban sa IBM Quantum hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payload for these initial steps is a small Bell state circuit chosen to be fast and inexpensive to run.\n"
msgstr "Ang payload para sa mga paunang hakbang na ito ay isang maliit na Bell state circuit na pinili dahil mabilis at mura itong patakbuhin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These examples use hardware because they demonstrate remote resource allocation and job management. A local circuit simulator does not validate the QRMI service and scheduler integration. Running this notebook submits IBM Quantum jobs and requires access to the configured backend.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ng hardware ang mga halimbawang ito dahil ipinapakita nila ang remote resource allocation at job management. Ang isang local circuit simulator ay hindi nagpapatunay ng integrasyon ng QRMI service at scheduler. Ang pagpapatakbo ng notebook na ito ay nagsusumite ng mga IBM Quantum job at nangangailangan ng access sa configured na backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map the classical problem to a quantum resource {#step-1-map-the-classical-problem-to-a-quantum-resource}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: I-map ang classical problem sa isang quantum resource {#step-1-map-the-classical-problem-to-a-quantum-resource}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first step in any QRMI workflow is to create a `QuantumResource` object and verify that it is accessible.\n"
msgstr "Ang unang hakbang sa anumang QRMI workflow ay ang paggawa ng `QuantumResource` object at pagpapatunay na naa-access ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`get_target()` retrieves the backend's hardware description (qubit count, basis gates, coupling map) and packages it as a Qiskit `Target` object, which the transpiler uses in Step 2.\n"
msgstr "Kinukuha ng `get_target()` ang hardware description ng backend (bilang ng qubit, basis gates, coupling map) at ibinabalot ito bilang isang Qiskit `Target` object, na ginagamit ng transpiler sa Hakbang 2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize the problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before submission, use Qiskit to transpile the circuit to the backend's instruction set architecture (ISA), using the `Target` object retrieved in Step 1.\n"
msgstr "Bago magsumite, gamitin ang Qiskit upang i-transpile ang circuit patungo sa instruction set architecture (ISA) ng backend, gamit ang `Target` object na nakuha sa Hakbang 1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example then builds a `Payload.QiskitPrimitive`, which wraps the OpenQASM 3 circuit string and job metadata into the IBM primitive schema.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos ay bumubuo ang halimbawa ng `Payload.QiskitPrimitive`, na binabalot ang OpenQASM 3 circuit string at job metadata sa loob ng IBM primitive schema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using QRMI primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qrmi-primitives}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Isagawa gamit ang QRMI primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qrmi-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the payload built, the example submits the job and polls for completion. `task_start()` returns a job ID immediately; `task_status()` is polled until the status is no longer `Queued`/`Running`. Results are retrieved as a raw JSON string and parsed to extract measurement samples.\n"
msgstr "Matapos mabuo ang payload, isinusumite ng halimbawa ang job at nagpo-poll para sa completion. Agad na nagbabalik ang `task_start()` ng job ID; pino-poll ang `task_status()` hanggang hindi na `Queued`/`Running` ang status. Ang mga resulta ay kinukuha bilang raw JSON string at pino-parse upang makuha ang mga measurement sample.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following cell keeps acquisition, execution, and cleanup together so that failures after acquisition still release a notebook-owned session.\n"
msgstr "Pinapanatili ng sumusunod na cell ang acquisition, execution, at cleanup nang magkasama upang ang mga kabiguan pagkatapos ng acquisition ay mag-release pa rin ng session na pag-aari ng notebook.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Higher-level Qiskit interface: QRMIService and SamplerV2 {#higher-level-qiskit-interface-qrmiservice-and-samplerv2}"
msgstr "Mas mataas na antas na Qiskit interface: QRMIService at SamplerV2 {#higher-level-qiskit-interface-qrmiservice-and-samplerv2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The raw lifecycle above provides explicit control over every call. For standard Qiskit workflows, QRMI provides a `SamplerV2` primitive implementing `BaseSamplerV2`.\n"
msgstr "Ang raw lifecycle sa itaas ay nagbibigay ng eksplisitong kontrol sa bawat tawag. Para sa mga standard na Qiskit workflow, nagbibigay ang QRMI ng `SamplerV2` primitive na nagpapatupad ng `BaseSamplerV2`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Lifecycle management\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Pamamahala ng lifecycle\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`SamplerV2` handles payload serialization, submission (`task_start`), polling, and result decoding. In an HPC batch setting (for example, with Slurm), allocation and release are managed by the scheduler and the SPANK plugin. In an interactive Python session using direct low-level API objects, `acquire()` and `release()` can be used to explicitly manage dedicated sessions.\n"
msgstr "Hinahawakan ng `SamplerV2` ang payload serialization, submission (`task_start`), polling, at result decoding. Sa isang HPC batch setting (halimbawa, gamit ang Slurm), ang allocation at release ay pinamamahalaan ng scheduler at ng SPANK plugin. Sa isang interactive na Python session na gumagamit ng direktang low-level na API object, maaaring gamitin ang `acquire()` at `release()` upang eksplisitong pamahalaan ang mga dedicated session.\n"

