# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example: SQD on N$_2$ {#large-scale-hardware-example-sqd-on-n-2}"
msgstr "Malaking halimbawa sa hardware: SQD sa N$_2$ {#large-scale-hardware-example-sqd-on-n-2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we put all components together into a complete quantum chemistry workflow at a larger scale, executed on real IBM Quantum hardware through QRMI.\n"
msgstr "Dito pinagsasama-sama natin ang lahat ng bahagi sa isang kumpletong quantum chemistry workflow sa mas malaking sukat, na isinagawa sa aktwal na IBM Quantum hardware sa pamamagitan ng QRMI.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**SQD** combines the following:\n"
"1. Quantum sampling of a Local Unitary Cluster Jastrow (LUCJ) ansatz constructed using `ffsim` and initialized from CCSD amplitudes\n"
"2. Hardware-aware transpilation matching the heavy-hex lattice topology via `generate_lucj_pass_manager`\n"
"3. Sampling execution on IBM Quantum hardware managed through `QRMIService` and QRMI `SamplerV2`\n"
"4. Classical post-processing: self-consistent configuration recovery and iterative subspace diagonalization using `qiskit-addon-sqd`\n"
msgstr ""
"Pinagsasama ng **SQD** ang mga sumusunod:\n"
"1. Quantum sampling ng isang Local Unitary Cluster Jastrow (LUCJ) ansatz na binuo gamit ang `ffsim` at ini-initialize mula sa CCSD amplitude\n"
"2. Hardware-aware transpilation na tumutugma sa heavy-hex lattice topology sa pamamagitan ng `generate_lucj_pass_manager`\n"
"3. Sampling execution sa IBM Quantum hardware na pinamamahalaan sa pamamagitan ng `QRMIService` at QRMI `SamplerV2`\n"
"4. Classical post-processing: self-consistent configuration recovery at iterative subspace diagonalization gamit ang `qiskit-addon-sqd`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We apply SQD to N$_2$ at a bond distance of 1.0 $\\AA$ with an active space derived from the `cc-pVDZ` basis set (26 spatial orbitals, corresponding to 52 spin-orbitals/qubits).\n"
msgstr "Inilalapat natin ang SQD sa N$_2$ sa bond distance na 1.0 $\\AA$ na may active space na hinango mula sa `cc-pVDZ` basis set (26 spatial orbitals, katumbas ng 52 spin-orbitals/qubits).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Reference energy for N$_2$ /cc-pVDZ active space (bond distance 1.0 $\\AA$):**\n"
"- Reference energy (separate SCI calculation): **−109.22802922 Ha**\n"
msgstr ""
"**Reference energy para sa N$_2$ /cc-pVDZ active space (bond distance 1.0 $\\AA$):**\n"
"- Reference energy (hiwalay na SCI calculation): **−109.22802922 Ha**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Accuracy of the saved run\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Katumpakan ng naka-save na run\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The SQD run below demonstrates successful end-to-end QRMI execution on IBM Quantum hardware. With a single LUCJ repetition and 100,000 shots the result finishes approximately 23.7 kcal/mol above the reference energy and does not achieve chemical accuracy (≤ 1 kcal/mol). Changing `n_reps`, the shot count, or the number of SQD iterations might improve accuracy, but requires further testing.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng SQD run sa ibaba ang matagumpay na end-to-end na QRMI execution sa IBM Quantum hardware. Gamit ang iisang LUCJ repetition at 100,000 shots, natatapos ang resulta nang humigit-kumulang 23.7 kcal/mol sa itaas ng reference energy at hindi nakakamit ang chemical accuracy (≤ 1 kcal/mol). Ang pagbabago ng `n_reps`, ng shot count, o ng bilang ng SQD iteration ay maaaring magpabuti ng katumpakan, ngunit nangangailangan ito ng karagdagang pagsubok.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the saved run, the `ffsim` pass manager removed the opposite-spin interactions `(24, 24)` and `(20, 20)` because the backend could not accommodate them. The reported results use this adjusted circuit.\n"
msgstr "Sa naka-save na run, inalis ng `ffsim` pass manager ang mga opposite-spin interaction na `(24, 24)` at `(20, 20)` dahil hindi ito kayang tanggapin ng backend. Ginagamit ng iniulat na mga resulta ang naayos na circuit na ito.\n"

